Hello. Thankyou for using synhxd.

This is the server package. It does not have the code or ability to compile
client software. If you wish to compile the client software, please download
shx.

Synapse Hotline X Daemon (synhxd or synHXD) is an hxd server with
modifications. All modifications were made by Devin Teske (aka. Synapse).

Right now, the version numbering is still based off of hxd's version where Ror
left off (if you don't know by now, hxd has been abandoned by it's creator(s)).

Eventually, it will stem off into it's own version numbering system and the end
product will be a server that will be compatible with all the latest servers
(plus it will have a crap load more features than those other ones).

I am not promising a truly unique and awesome server, i am just saying i have
some excellent ideas.

You can contact the author (Devin) at:

devinteske@hotmail.com


Technical info...

Files that were modifed in synhxd over hxd-0.1.41 (Ror released 0.1.41 in cvs):
acconfig.h           accounts.c            banlist               commands.c
config.h.in          configure.in          files.c               hotline.h
hlserver.c           hlwrite.c             htxf.c                hxd.c
hxd.conf             hxd.h                 hxd_config.c          news
rcv.c                version.c
